<h1 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Panama's Role in the World – Lesson # 3</h1>
<p style="text-align: center;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Role in the World</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How the Canal Impacts Panama's Future</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Present an analysis of a current issue, local or global. Interactive: Conduct interviews on various topics, including current events, academic topics, and past experiences.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can present an analysis of the Panama Canal's impact during the 2023 drought to explain decisions (e.g., "New regulations were imposed to limit the number of daily crossings to conserve water.")
Can conduct interviews on global trade topics, asking about the Canal's effects on trade (e.g., "How has the Panama Canal impacted global trade?" "If Panama had not built the Canal, global trade would have faced significant challenges in the early 20th century.")
Can summarize responses from interviews, focusing on the economic impact of the Canal (e.g., "It was explained that without the Panama Canal, shipping would have been slower and more costly.")</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a world map showing major shipping routes and highlights the Panama Canal. Students are asked to verbally identify countries that would be impacted if the Canal faced operational challenges. The teacher asks, "How would the global economy be affected if the Panama Canal experienced severe delays?" encouraging initial thoughts and using previously learned vocabulary related to "shipping" and "trade."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary from the previous lesson, focusing on words with the long /oʊ/ sound like "global," "local," "boat," "show," and multisyllabic words with full and reduced vowels such as "environmental" /ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.təl/ and "impactful" /ɪmˈpækt.fəl/. The teacher explains how to express hypothetical ideas using conditional sentences, for example: "If Panama had not built the Canal, global trade would have faced significant challenges."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding by asking:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a ship normally takes 20 days and now takes 30 days, are there 'delays' or 'efficiency'?" (Expected answer: delays)</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the difference between 'shipping' and 'trade'?" (Expected answer: Shipping is the transport, trade is the exchange of goods.)</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio excerpt (approx. 1-2 minutes) from a news report or podcast discussing the 2023 drought and its impact on the Panama Canal's "operation," "traffic," and "shipping costs." The register is informative and academic, suitable for discussing a "global" issue. It includes examples of "passive voice" (e.g., "The number of daily crossings was significantly reduced.") and "Present Perfect Continuous" (e.g., "The Canal has been adjusting its regulations to conserve water.").</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening for specific information to understand the impact of current events on global trade and Panama's infrastructure.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Speaking focus):</b> After listening, students verbally answer gist and detail questions in pairs:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"According to the report, what has been happening to the Canal's 'operation' lately?" (Gist)</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific measures have 'been imposed' by the 'authority' to manage water levels?" (Detail, passive voice practice)</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has this situation been 'impacting' global 'shipping'?" (Detail, present perfect continuous practice)</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Practicing speaking using passive voice, second and third conditionals, and present perfect continuous, along with the target vocabulary (e.g., "congestion," "efficiency," "investments," "environmental groups," "influence," "speculate," "affect"). Pronunciation focus on /oʊ/ and multisyllabic words.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion (5 min):</b> Students receive sentences with blanks that require a verb in the passive voice, a conditional clause, or the present perfect continuous tense, using target vocabulary. E.g., "The Canal ______ (manage) by the ACP since 1999." "If the drought ______ (not affect) the Canal, 'global trade' ______ (not face) such 'delays'." "Recently, the 'government' ______ (invest) in 'infrastructure' improvements." Students complete the sentences orally in pairs, then share their answers with the class, focusing on accurate pronunciation.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Chain Story (8 min):</b> The teacher starts a sentence about the Canal using one of the target grammatical structures, e.g., "The Panama Canal has been vital for global shipping, but it has also been causing environmental concerns." The first student in a row must add a related sentence using a conditional or passive voice (e.g., "If significant investments had been made in new technologies, perhaps traffic congestion would be less severe."). The next student adds another sentence, continuing the narrative. This encourages spontaneous use of the target language.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - "What If...?" Discussion (7 min):</b> Students work in pairs. Each student receives a set of incomplete hypothetical questions related to the Canal's future and its "influence" on "global relationships." E.g., "What if the Canal had been built in a different location? How would global trade have been impacted?" "If the Canal's 'efficiency' continues to improve, what might 'speculate' about Panama's future 'investments'?" They complete the questions and then take turns asking and answering, using second and third conditionals and summarizing their partner's "speculations."</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Canal Impact Interview Panel." Students work in groups of 4. Two students act as "Journalists" (interviewers), one acts as a "Panama Canal Authority (ACP) Representative," and one acts as an "Environmental Expert." The Journalists' role is to conduct an interview about the Canal's impact during the recent drought and its future implications. The ACP Representative and Environmental Expert must articulate their perspectives, explaining past decisions and future plans, and speculating on hypothetical scenarios. Journalists must summarize the responses at the end.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> The interview questions will directly address "How the Canal Impacts Panama's Future" and "Panama's Role in the World." For example, Journalists might ask: "How has the 'Panama Canal Authority' been 'adjusting' its 'operation' due to the drought?" "If the 'government' had not made 'investments' in water conservation, how would 'shipping' routes be affected today?" "What 'environmental concerns' have 'been raised' by 'environmental groups' regarding the Canal's expansion?"</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus on Fluency and Interaction:</b> Students are encouraged to use the target grammar (passive voice, second and third conditionals, present perfect continuous) and vocabulary naturally. Journalists should ask follow-up questions, and interviewees should provide detailed answers, expressing hypothetical ideas and discussing the Canal's "impact" and "influence" respectfully, using appropriate trade-related terms. The emphasis is on continuous, meaningful spoken interaction.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation using a checklist focusing on the application of target grammatical structures and vocabulary in spoken interaction, complemented by peer assessment.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform the "Canal Impact Interview Panel" (from Stage 4). Journalists will present a brief oral summary (1 minute) of the key points and differing perspectives gathered from their interviews, focusing on the economic impact of the Canal.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation, especially of /oʊ/ and multisyllabic words like "environmental," "impactful."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Appropriate and accurate use of words like "operation," "congestion," "investments," "authority," "speculate," "affect," "impact," "influence."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and coherence:</b> Ideas are expressed clearly and logically, especially when presenting an analysis or expressing hypothetical ideas.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Application of target grammar:</b> Accurate use of passive voice, second and third conditionals, and present perfect continuous.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration and Interaction:</b> Effective turn-taking, asking relevant questions, and providing detailed responses.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts:
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new idea I learned about the Canal's 'future' or 'impact' today was..."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Using conditionals to 'speculate' about the Canal's challenges was easy / somewhat challenging / very challenging because..."</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
          <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's speaking activities helped me most to discuss the Canal's 'influence'?"</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do I feel now discussing hypothetical situations related to 'global trade' and the Canal?"</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The "Canal Impact Interview Panel" worked well to encourage interactive speaking and the use of complex grammatical structures. The chain story activity effectively prompted immediate application of the target grammar. Some students needed more scaffolding for forming third conditionals spontaneously. Future lessons should reinforce this through additional guided practice. I noticed consistent challenges with the full pronunciation of multisyllabic words for some students, which needs continued attention.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The summaries and analyses presented in this speaking lesson will serve as a foundation for Lesson 4 (Writing Composition), where students will write a formal analysis or opinion piece about the Canal's future impact, incorporating the grammatical structures and vocabulary practiced today.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">___ min</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>